{"path":"cargo/getting-started/first-steps.html","title":"First Steps with Cargo","description":"This section provides a quick sense for the cargo command line tool. We demonstrate its ability to generate a new package for us, its ability to compile the crate within the package, and its ability…","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"first-steps-with-cargo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First Steps with Cargo"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This section provides a quick sense for the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo"},{"type":"text","value":" command line tool. We demonstrate its ability to generate a new "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#package","title":"\"package\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"package"}]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" for us, its ability to compile the "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#crate","title":"\"crate\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"crate"}]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" within the package, and its ability to run the resulting program."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To start a new package with Cargo, use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo new"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo new hello_world"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo defaults to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--bin"},{"type":"text","value":" to make a binary program. To make a library, we would pass "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--lib"},{"type":"text","value":", instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let’s check out what Cargo has generated for us:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cd hello_world\n$ tree .\n.\n├── Cargo.toml\n└── src\n    └── main.rs\n\n1 directory, 2 files"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is all we need to get started. First, let’s check out "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[package]\nname = \"hello_world\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[dependencies]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is called a "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#manifest","title":"\"manifest\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"manifest"}]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":", and it contains all of the metadata that Cargo needs to compile your package."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here’s what’s in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"src/main.rs"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"rust","code":"fn main() {\n    println!(\"Hello, world!\");\n}"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo generated a “hello world” program for us, otherwise known as a "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#crate","title":"\"crate\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"binary crate"}]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":". Let’s compile it:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo build\n   Compiling hello_world v0.1.0 (file:///path/to/package/hello_world)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And then run it:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ ./target/debug/hello_world\nHello, world!"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We can also use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo run"},{"type":"text","value":" to compile and then run it, all in one step:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo run\n     Fresh hello_world v0.1.0 (file:///path/to/package/hello_world)\n   Running `target/hello_world`\nHello, world!"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"going-further","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Going further"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more details on using Cargo, check out the "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/guide/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo Guide"}]}]}]}}
